Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 15:16:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: consolidate Course page init into single GET
 /courses/:id call
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wires the Course page to the new aggregate backend response
{ course, videos, enrollment, progress } instead of three separate
requests + a per-video loop. Only data-fetching changed — no UI,
layout, or unrelated (quiz/assignment) logic touched.

- services/courseService.ts: fetchCourseById now parses the aggregate
  shape and flattens it into CourseDetail (course fields spread at
  top level for backward compat with existing courseData.* access,
  plus new enrollment/progress/videos[].position fields). Added
  CourseEnrollment type; reused VideoProgress from quizService instead
  of inventing a new shape.
- lib/mock/course.ts: mockCourse gets enrollment + progress fields so
  the mock-course path (isMockCourse) matches the new CourseDetail
  shape and preserves its previous 'always enrolled' demo behavior.
- store/slices/quizSlice.ts: added hydrateVideoProgress, a plain
  reducer that bulk-sets videoProgressMap from progress[] in one
  dispatch. Same state shape consumers already read (videoProgressMap,
  getVideoProgress) — no new store/slice.
- app/course/[id]/page.tsx:
  - Removed the checkEnrollmentStatus call from Course init; isEnrolled
    now comes from data.enrollment on the aggregate response.
  - Removed the per-video dispatch(fetchVideoProgress(videoId)) inside
    checkVideoAndQuizStatus; replaced with one
    dispatch(hydrateVideoProgress(data.progress)) after course load.
    Quiz-status and assignment-status per-video fetches are untouched
    (out of scope).
  - Added a useRef guard so a duplicate GET /courses/:id can't fire for
    the same courseId if the init effect re-runs.
- components/enrollment-card.tsx: removed its own independent
  checkEnrollmentStatus call (a second, previously-unnoticed source of
  redundant enrollment requests on every Course page load) — it now
  just uses the isEnrolled prop from the parent, which already carries
  the aggregate response's enrollment data.

Net result on Course page load: exactly one network request for
course + videos + enrollment + progress (verified by reading the
call graph — enrollment-card.tsx was the second hidden source of a
duplicate request). Quiz/assignment fetches (out of scope) unchanged.
No N+1: all four are read from the same single course-controller
Prisma query on the backend.

Verified with tsc --noEmit (clean) and next lint (clean on all
touched files). Full 'next build' hits an unrelated sandbox network
restriction (Google Fonts fetch), not a compile error in this change.
